  "note": "Hand-written expectations of the public fixtures' page media and ink alternatives, for tests/content.rs. Each field is a JSON pointer into one page line, the field kind it is checked under, and the value the CLI writes there when it holds what onenote_parser's API gives for the record: the same values tests/media.rs and tests/ink.rs assert, written by hand from that API, not from the CLI's output. A null value is a field the page must not have. A page is found by its id in the read of each of its files. A page's media come in the order the reader visits them: its containers in stored order, each outline's blocks in order, then the page's own ink drawing. Left out: the SVG drawings' names and strokes (tests/ink.rs), and the page's text, its runs, lists, tables and tags (tests/markdown.rs, and the unit tests in src/content.rs and src/markdown.rs).",
